/T (individually to the original list. C. Both append\(\) and extend\(\) methods will add their contents in the same way by creating a nested list inside the original list. D. The append\(\) method replaces the existing list, and extend\(\) clears the list before adding the new sequence. Correct Answer: B Explanation: The append\(\) method adds its argument as a single element to the end of the list, even if it's another list or sequence, whereas the extend\(\) method iterates over the elements of its argument and adds them to the original list individually.)
