/T (A. elif allows for multiple, specific conditions to be checked, each with its own code block, following an if statement. B. elif is used to terminate loops when a condition is met. C. elif can be used independently of an if statement to check conditions. D. There is no difference; elif and else are interchangeable. Correct Answer: A Explanation: elif stands for "else if," and it allows a program to check multiple different conditions after an initial if statement. Each elif must have its own condition, providing a way to handle more than just two possible outcomes \(true or false\) like with a simple if-else structure.)
/E (A. elif allows for multiple, specific conditions to be checked, each with its own code block, following an if statement. B. elif is used to terminate loops when a condition is met. C. elif can be used independently of an if statement to check conditions. D. There is no difference; elif and else are interchangeable. Correct Answer: A Explanation: elif stands for "else if," and it allows a program to check multiple different conditions after an initial if statement. Each elif must have its own condition, providing a way to handle more than just two possible outcomes \(true or false\) like with a simple if-else structure.)
