/T (Question 4. What does the break statement do within a loop in Python? A. It exits the current loop and resumes execution at the next statement outside of the loop. B. It skips the current iteration and moves directly to the next iteration within the loop. C. It temporarily pauses the loop execution and resumes only when a specified condition changes. D. It restarts the loop from the first line with the original condition. Correct Answer: A Explanation: The break statement is used to exit a loop prematurely when a certain condition is met. This is particularly useful when searching for an item that meets specific criteria in a list or when an external condition triggers the termination of the loop.)
