/T (Question 2. When a Python function has a default argument, what happens if the caller does not provide a value for that argument, and how does this feature help streamline function calls, reducing redundancy in the code? A. The function will raise an error. B. The default value specified is used if no argument is passed. C. The function will ignore that argument and not return anything. D. The function will call another function to handle missing arguments. Correct Answer: B Explanation: Default arguments in Python allow a function to use a predefined value when no value is provided during the function call. This reduces redundancy in code by eliminating the need to repeatedly pass the same value in every call.)
