/T (Question 8. What is the role of the global keyword in Python functions, and how does it enable a function to modify variables that are defined outside of its scope, particularly in cases where you want to modify a global variable from within a function? A. It allows a function to define new variables only inside its local scope. B. It makes the function's variables global, affecting all other functions. C. It allows a function to access and modify a variable from the global scope. D. It is used to restrict functions from accessing global variables. Correct Answer: C Explanation: The global keyword allows a function to access and modify a variable that is defined in the global scope. Without global, Python would treat the variable as local to the function, and changes would not reflect in the global scope.)
