/T (Question 22. In a Python dictionary, which of the following operations is expected to have an average time complexity of O\(1\), and why? A. Inserting a new key-value pair B. Accessing a value by its key C. Deleting an existing key D. All of the above Correct Answer: D Explanation: Python dictionaries are implemented using hash tables. Both insertion, access, and deletion operations typically run in O\(1\) time on average due to efficient hash-based indexing. However, in the worst case \(e.g., hash collisions\), these operations can degrade to O\(n\), but such cases are rare.)
