/T (Question 52. When using a dictionary in Python, which method would you use to retrieve the value associated with a specific key, while also providing a default value that will be returned if the key is not found in the dictionary, thus preventing a KeyError from being raised? A. get\(\) B. fetch\(\) C. retrieve\(\) D. obtain\(\) Correct Answer: A Explanation: The get\(\) method of a dictionary is used to access the value associated with a given key. If the key does not exist, it returns None by default, but you can specify a different default value to return instead. This functionality makes get\(\) a safe way to access dictionary values without raising exceptions for missing keys, unlike directly accessing a key that may not exist.)
