/T (Question 24. In Python, when creating a new class, you can define special methods to customize the behavior of its instances. One commonly used special method is __init__, which is responsible for object initialization. However, there are other dunder \(double underscore\) methods as well. Which of the following correctly describes the purpose and use of the __str__ method within Python's OOP, and what its output is expected to represent? A. The __str__ method is used to return a string representation of the object, typically for user-friendly output purposes. B. The __str__ method is responsible for initializing an object and must always return a dictionary of attributes. C. The __str__ method is used to define custom operators for objects, allowing comparison between instances. D. The __str__ method is automatically called during object destruction to clean up memory resources. Correct Answer: A Explanation: The __str__ method is intended to provide a human-readable string representation of an object. It is automatically invoked when the print\(\) function is called on an object, making it useful for generating user- friendly output, as opposed to the __repr__ method, which is more for debugging.)
/E (Question 24. In Python, when creating a new class, you can define special methods to customize the behavior of its instances. One commonly used special method is __init__, which is responsible for object initialization. However, there are other dunder \(double underscore\) methods as well. Which of the following correctly describes the purpose and use of the __str__ method within Python's OOP, and what its output is expected to represent? A. The __str__ method is used to return a string representation of the object, typically for user-friendly output purposes. B. The __str__ method is responsible for initializing an object and must always return a dictionary of attributes. C. The __str__ method is used to define custom operators for objects, allowing comparison between instances. D. The __str__ method is automatically called during object destruction to clean up memory resources. Correct Answer: A Explanation: The __str__ method is intended to provide a human-readable string representation of an object. It is automatically invoked when the print\(\) function is called on an object, making it useful for generating user- friendly output, as opposed to the __repr__ method, which is more for debugging.)
