/T (Question 45. In Python, if a class has a method that is defined in a parent class but overridden in a child class, and the child class method has the same name and parameters but a different implementation, which of the following object-oriented principles is this an example of? How does this principle allow for more flexible and dynamic behavior in class hierarchies? A. Method Overriding B. Method Overloading C. Encapsulation D. Polymorphism Correct Answer: A Explanation: Method overriding occurs when a child class provides a specific implementation for a method that is already defined in its parent class. This allows the child class to modify or extend the behavior of the inherited method, providing more flexibility in class hierarchies.)
/E (Question 45. In Python, if a class has a method that is defined in a parent class but overridden in a child class, and the child class method has the same name and parameters but a different implementation, which of the following object-oriented principles is this an example of? How does this principle allow for more flexible and dynamic behavior in class hierarchies? A. Method Overriding B. Method Overloading C. Encapsulation D. Polymorphism Correct Answer: A Explanation: Method overriding occurs when a child class provides a specific implementation for a method that is already defined in its parent class. This allows the child class to modify or extend the behavior of the inherited method, providing more flexibility in class hierarchies.)
